---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: author.name,
    section: "Protein Powder Rankings",
    tags: [
      "meijer protein powder",
      "best meijer protein powder",
      "meijer whey protein",
      "meijer brand protein powder",
      "protein powder at meijer"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <ArticleHeader kicker={"Buyer's Guide"} badge={"Label-Checked"} author={author} dates={dates} mobileAd={false}>
      <Fragment slot="title">Best Meijer Protein Powder</Fragment>
      What the Midwest supercenter chain actually stocks, whether its own Meijer-brand whey is worth buying, and six picks ranked by how much protein you get for your money.
    </ArticleHeader>

    <TableOfContents>
      <a href="#short-answer">The Short Answer</a>
      <a href="#what-meijer-sells">What Meijer Sells</a>
      <a href="#top-picks">Our Top Picks</a>
      <a href="#meijer-brand">Meijer's Own Whey</a>
      <a href="#cost-per-25g">Cost per 25 g</a>
      <a href="#testing">Third-Party Testing</a>
      <a href="#where-cheapest">Store vs Online</a>
      <a href="#other-options">Plant, Clear and Gainer</a>
      <a href="#vs-other-stores">Meijer vs Other Stores</a>
      <a href="#which-to-buy">Which to Buy</a>
      <a href="#mistakes">Common Mistakes</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </TableOfContents>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          The best Meijer protein powder for most shoppers is Meijer's own whey: 30 g of protein per serving, per the label, for $26.99 a 2 lb tub, which works out to roughly $1.15 per 25 g of protein. That is cheaper per gram than every name brand we found on Meijer's shelf. Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard is the pick if you want a sport-certified whey, and Orgain is the dairy-free option. Below we explain what Meijer stocks, how the house brand reads label by label, and how to check the cost per 25 g yourself in the aisle.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Meijer Protein Powder: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            Meijer's own-brand whey is the cheapest way to buy protein at Meijer, at about $1.15 per 25 g of protein. It is a plain, sweetened whey concentrate and isolate blend with no third-party certification we could find, so it suits recreational lifters who want the lowest price. If you want a certified product, Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard in the 3.89 lb tub costs a little more per gram and has two flavors listed in NSF's Certified for Sport registry. Body Fortress and Premier Protein sit in between on price, Isopure is the lean isolate, and Orgain is the plant pick.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Powder (size at Meijer)</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Protein / serving</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Meijer price seen</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Cost per 25 g</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Meijer Whey Protein (2 lb)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">30 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$26.99</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About $1.12-1.19</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">ON Gold Standard 100% Whey (3.89 lb)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">24 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$79.59</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About $1.45-1.50</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Body Fortress Super Advanced Whey (1.78 lb)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">30 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$32.99</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About $1.53</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Premier Protein 100% Whey (17 servings)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">30 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$35.99</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About $1.76</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Orgain Organic Protein (about 1 lb)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">21 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$20.99</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About $2.50</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Isopure Zero Carb (14 servings)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">25 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$36.99</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About $2.64</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            Prices in the table are the regular prices shown on Meijer.com product listings in November 2026 and vary by store. Protein figures are per the label at the time of writing and vary by flavor. The cost section below shows exactly how each figure was worked out, so you can redo the sum with your own store's shelf tag.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="what-meijer-sells" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. What Protein Powder Does Meijer Sell?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Meijer sells a mid-sized supplement aisle of mainstream sports and grocery brands, plus its own Meijer-brand whey. Meijer runs more than 250 supercenters across Michigan, Ohio, Indiana, Illinois, Kentucky and Wisconsin, and its protein section looks like a cross between a Walmart and a grocery store: fewer budget giants than Walmart, more than a typical supermarket. Meijer.com's protein powder category listed several dozen items when we checked, and a site search for protein powder returned well over a hundred results once shakes and bars were included.
          </p>

          <p>
            The whey brands we found on Meijer.com listings were Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard (1.5 lb and 3.89 lb tubs), Body Fortress Super Advanced Whey and its 100% Isolate, Premier Protein powder, Isopure Zero Carb and Low Carb, Dymatize ISO100, and Jocko Mölk (a 2 lb tub listed at $46.99). Clear whey shows up too, with listings for Oath Clear Protein and WICKED Protein. For plant protein, Meijer.com lists several Orgain organic tubs, including a 30 g vegan version, and Orgain's Justin's nut-butter protein. Delivery apps that shop Meijer stores also list Vega Protein and Greens, OWYN and Muscle Milk Pro Series.
          </p>

          <p>
            Stock is the catch. Several of the Meijer.com pages we looked at marked one flavor in stock and another out of stock, or showed low stock at a particular store. A big supercenter in the Detroit or Grand Rapids suburbs will carry far more than a smaller store, so check the Meijer app with your store selected before making a special trip. The brand list above is what Meijer carries across its range, not a promise that every store has every tub.
          </p>

          <p>
            What Meijer does not stock, as far as we could find, are the premium direct-to-consumer brands such as Levels, Transparent Labs or Ascent's full range. If those are your brands, you will be ordering online whatever store you shop at. For the brands Meijer does carry, our reviews of <a href="/optimum-nutrition-protein-powder-review/">Optimum Nutrition</a>, <a href="/body-fortress-protein-powder-review/">Body Fortress</a> and <a href="/premier-protein-powder-review/">Premier Protein</a> go deeper on each label.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. The Best Protein Powders at Meijer
          </h2>

          <p>
            These six powders all appeared on Meijer.com product listings when we checked in November 2026. They are ranked by value first (cost per 25 g of protein at Meijer's listed price), then by label quality and certification. Prices are snapshots and vary by store, flavor and week; label figures are per the label at the time of writing and vary by flavor. We built the ranking from labels and listings, not from tasting the powders.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <ProductCard product={product} rank={index + 1} />
          ))}
        </div>

        <div id="meijer-brand" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Does Meijer Have Its Own Protein Powder?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Yes. Meijer sells a Meijer-brand whey protein powder in 2 lb tubs, and Meijer.com has a collection page for Meijer-brand protein. We found listings for Vanilla and Chocolate at $26.99 each, a 32 oz Whey Protein Power Blend in Chocolate Peanut Butter at the same $26.99, and product records for Strawberry and Cookies and Cream. Meijer does not name the manufacturer on the listings we could see, and we could not confirm who makes it, so we judge it on the label alone.
          </p>

          <p>
            Per the label as recorded at the time of writing, a serving of the vanilla tub is about 44 g and gives 30 g of protein, about 180 calories, 7 g of carbohydrate, 3 g of sugar and 3 g of fat. The Chocolate Peanut Butter Power Blend lists a 48 g serving with 30 g of protein and about 190 calories. Those figures come from the panel copied into public food databases and from Meijer's own listing, so read the panel on your tub, because store-brand recipes do change between production runs.
          </p>

          <p>
            The ingredient list is a typical budget whey. The protein is a blend of whey concentrate and whey isolate, followed by maltodextrin, modified food starch and dextrose, then gums, flavors, and the sweeteners acesulfame potassium and sucralose. One older vanilla label we found also listed sugar and soy lecithin, and the chocolate peanut butter version lists soy lecithin, so check for soy if that matters to you. All versions contain milk.
          </p>

          <p>
            The fillers explain why a 30 g protein serving needs 44 to 48 g of powder. Roughly two-thirds of each scoop is protein, against about three-quarters for Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard. That is fine for a post-workout shake, but it means a few more carbs and calories per gram of protein than a leaner whey. For most people buying on price, it is a fair trade for the lowest cost per gram in the store.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-3">THE HOUSE-BRAND VERDICT</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Cheapest protein per dollar at Meijer, with no certification we could find.</p>
            <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed m-0">Buy it for everyday shakes if you are not drug-tested and are happy with sucralose. Skip it if you compete in tested sport, avoid artificial sweeteners, or want a short ingredient list.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="cost-per-25g" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            5. How Much Does Protein Powder Cost at Meijer per 25 g?
          </h2>

          <p>
            At Meijer's listed prices, protein powder costs about $1.12 to $2.64 per 25 g of protein, depending on the brand. The house brand is cheapest and the small Isopure tub is the most expensive. We use cost per 25 g because 25 g is roughly one solid serving of protein, and because it is the only fair way to compare a 2 lb tub of 30 g servings with a 14-serving tub of 25 g servings.
          </p>

          <p>
            The sum is simple. Multiply the servings per container by the grams of protein per serving to get the total protein in the tub. Divide the price by that total, then multiply by 25. For the Meijer vanilla whey, a 907 g tub with a 44 g serving holds about 20 servings, so about 600 g of protein. $26.99 divided by 600, times 25, is about $1.12. The heavier 48 g serving in the peanut butter blend gives about 19 servings and closer to $1.19.
