          <p>
            Size matters as much as brand. Optimum Nutrition's 1.47 lb chocolate tub was listed at $35.99 on Meijer.com, which is roughly 20 servings of 24 g and about $1.87 per 25 g, while the 3.89 lb tub drops to about $1.45 to $1.50. The small Isopure tub at $36.99 is the clearest case: the same powder in a 3 lb tub costs far less per gram at most retailers, but Meijer's listings we saw were for the 14 to 16 serving size.
          </p>

          <p>
            One listing needs a caveat. Meijer.com titled its Premier Protein Vanilla Milkshake tub as 28 oz, but the same product code is listed at Kroger as a 23.3 oz tub of 17 servings, and Premier's labels we have seen give 17 servings. We used 17 servings of 30 g in the sum. If your tub says more, the cost per 25 g falls accordingly. Our <a href="/best-cheap-protein-powder/">cheapest protein powder guide</a> uses the same method across every brand we cover.
          </p>
